# SPA build-time env (Vite). Picked up by `vite build` (`npm run build` in
# bin/deploy-spa). NOT applied during `npm run dev`, which uses
# `.env.development` (absent → these vars are unset → the SPA renders the
# local dev-login picker instead of the Auth0 redirect flow).
#
# `VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN` non-empty + `VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID` non-empty enables
# the Auth0 SPA SDK gate (see `web/src/auth/auth0Provider.tsx`). The
# Client ID is public per Auth0 SPA conventions — safe to commit.
#
# Audience must match the API's `AUTH0_AUDIENCE` env (set in
# `infrastructure/lambda.tf` from the `auth0_audience` tofu var,
# default `xpool-api`).

VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN=xpool.ca.auth0.com
VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=O5fP2fX0RzYArKYjSDH2dxq9LGI5oG20
VITE_AUTH0_AUDIENCE=xpool-api
